{{Quote|Have your people transport everything back to Security Bureau headquarters.|[[Unidentified Imperial Security Bureau major|An ISB]] [[major]], to a [[Unidentified Coruscant Security captain (Imperial Security Bureau major)|captain]] of the [[Coruscant Security Force]] during an investigation into a [[Hunt for Jocasta Nu|bombing]]|<ref name="Vader 8">[[Darth Vader (2017) 8|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 8]]</ref>}}
The '''Imperial Security Bureau Central Office''',<ref name="Master of Evil">''[[Master of Evil]]''</ref> also known as the '''ISB Central Office''',<ref name="AbEverything" /> the '''Imperial Security Bureau headquarters''',<ref name="Inferno Squad">''[[Battlefront II: Inferno Squad]]''</ref> or '''ISB Headquarters''',<ref name="Dawn VG">''[[Star Wars: Dawn of Rebellion: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> was a massive complex the size of several [[city]] blocks that served as the headquarters of the [[Imperial Security Bureau]]<ref name="AbEverything" /> located within the [[COMPNOR arcology]] on [[Level 5127]] of the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]'s [[Federal District]].<ref name="Tarkin" />

It housed personnel and equipment to analyze intelligence data.<ref name="AbEverythingUE">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> The Central Office's staff of analysts had access to [[HoloNet]] feeds from across the Empire. While individual [[agent]]s had a great deal of discretion in resolving their assignments, the Central Office could reassign them as needed when higher-priority targets were identified. Most spend the majority of their time in the field, only returning to the Federal District between missions.<ref name="Dawn RPG">''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]''</ref> It operated throughout the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="Vader 8" />

==Description==
[[File:ISBFullMeeting-Andor4.png|thumb|left|290x290px|A meeting in the ISB Central Office]]
The ISB headquarters was a large pyramidoid building consisting of ten individual curved structures arranged in a circle around the main building, which itself was connected with the rest of the [[COMPNOR arcology|COMPNOR Arcology]] complex via transparent [[skybridge]]s. Its grounds were patrolled by Imperial [[stormtrooper]]s, while [[Point-defense laser cannon|point defence cannons]] lined the perimeter to deter airborne threats. Inside the main building there were conference chambers, at least one of which was used for sector supervisors' forums organized by Major [[Lio Partagaz|Partagaz]]<ref name="Aldhani" /> as well as announcements of significant policy changes, such as the implementation of the [[Public Order Resentencing Directive]] following the [[Aldhani heist|Aldhani incident]]. The [[ISB Supervisor]]s who attended [[ISB Board]] meetings in the room<ref name="Announcement" /> were part of the [[Investigations]] branch.<ref name="Dawn VG" />

Senior officers were afforded their own, albeit spartan, offices to share with their assistants. The building also housed a [[ISB datavault|datavault]] where data from all sectors under ISB supervision was stored and could be pulled for analysis by orders of the sector supervisor.<ref name="Announcement" /> The walls and floors were white<ref name="Aldhani" /> in stark contrast to typical Imperial design<ref name="World Building">{{InsiderCite|227|World Building (Star Wars Insider 227)}}</ref> and decorated with bright Imperial insignias.<ref name="Aldhani" /> The stark white coloration suggested ISB members saw themselves as ideologically pure.<ref name="World Building" /> Elsewhere in the building, there was at least one [[ISB interrogation room|interrogation room]], which was a brightly lit square room with a singular chair and three one-way mirrors on the walls. The room was surrounded by a dark room from which interrogations could be observed behind the glass.<ref name="Narkina 5" />

