==Behind the scenes==
[[File:ISBHeadquarters-2017DarthVader8.jpg|thumb|right|200px|The ISB Central Office in ''Darth Vader'' (2017) 8]]
The ISB Central Office was first mentioned in [[canon]] by the [[2015]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]'', written by [[Adam Bray]], [[Kerrie Dougherty]], [[Cole Horton]], and [[Michael Kogge]].<ref name="AbEverything" /> While two narrative sources state that the headquarters of ISB are located in the [[Federal District]],<ref name="Tarkin" /><ref name="Inferno Squad" /> the [[Fantasy Flight Games]]' [[2018]] [[roleplaying game]] book [[Dawn of Rebellion]] states that the headquarters are in the [[Verity District]].<ref name="Dawn RPG" /> This article assumes ''Dawn of Rebellion'' is in error.

The actual headquarters building made its first on screen appearance in "[[Aldhani]]," the fourth episode of the ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' television series.<ref name="Aldhani" /> Prior to the show's release, the set was shown being built in the sizzle reel for ''Andor''.<ref name="Sizzle">{{SWYouTube|gSW-pARyP-M|Sizzle Reel &#124; Andor &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/sizzle-andor}}</ref> The headquarters' exterior was photographed below Adams Bridge, Crossrail Plaza at the [[Wikipedia:Canary Wharf|Canary Wharf]] in [[Wikipedia:London|London]], [[Wikipedia:England|England]].<ref name="Episode Guide">{{SW|url=andor-s1-e9-trivia-gallery|text="Nobody's Listening!" Trivia Gallery &#124; Andor}} {{C|Slide 3}}</ref>

In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, [[ISB Central Office/Legends|ISB Central Office]] was first mentioned in the [[1989]] ''[[Imperial Sourcebook]]'', which was authored by [[Greg Gorden]] and published by [[West End Games]].<ref name="IS">''[[Imperial Sourcebook]]''</ref>

